cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this software or its findings, please cite it.
title: "meshlens: Serialization Order Confounds Attention Analysis in MeshXL"
abstract: >-
  Code, preregistrations, and run artifacts showing that attention in an
  autoregressive 3D mesh transformer tracks the order in which the mesh was
  serialized rather than the geometry of the mesh itself. In MeshXL's canonical
  serialization a face's index in the token stream predicts its vertical position
  at Spearman 0.951, so attention maps painted onto a mesh surface are confounded
  with plain recency before any causal question is asked.
type: software
